From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:06:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] fix(runtime): the game's malloc leaves a reserve for
 HLE allocations

The game's malloc/calloc/realloc (and the newlib _r forms) shared the
guest heap with the runtime's own allocations. SLES-55605 asks malloc
for ever smaller blocks until one fits, taking the whole heap for its
allocator; after that every guestMalloc failed, so libmpeg stream
callbacks were silently dropped, the movie player never got its audio
and stopped on the CRIWARE logo.

Allocations made for the game now leave 1 MiB (or a sixteenth of a
small heap) free; runtime-internal allocations may still use it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
